Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): stabilize unchanged host pickup observations
 [daveey]

Host-wide pickup bodies interpolated elapsed minutes, while _create deduplicated
watcher comments by exact body. Advancing one second over a minute boundary
therefore appended a third comment with no changed evidence. CI occurrences
34 and 35 ran merge sources ea4276f153d0364266ef6c0ee444bf0be6dd19d3 and
e30de1a0dd8270e3788edc7623b9c0bc4f693da2, both carrying this writer.

Render ready-since timestamps in the host-wide body; retain elapsed minutes in
the title and the existing target-refresh path. This is a production correction,
not a frozen-clock workaround. Force the boundary through the existing now
argument for all four causes and both 2/25 target cases. Verify real new skip
observations still append and unchanged replays do not. Retain moved-here clock
coverage against the actual replicated move timestamp.

Proof: baseline owning file 56 passed; deterministic old-writer RED 8 failed
(3 comments vs 2); GREEN owning file + incident suite 60 passed; all 16 test
files referencing kanban_pickup_stall 305 passed via hermes-core-wt test.
Full scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks passed, no health findings.
Raw CI and reproduction logs retained by task t_21bdb628627b563e.
